# A shell script with CRLF line endings does not run: `/bin/sh` reads the `\r`
# as part of the shebang's path and of every word after it. This repository is
# worked on from Windows, where the default `core.autocrlf=true` would hand out
# exactly that on checkout, so the one file it matters for is pinned.
*.sh text eol=lf
.githooks/* text eol=lf

# The stylesheet-patch test fixtures are signed bytes: `patch-sheet.sig.b64` is
# a minisign signature over `patch-sheet.css` exactly as it is here. A checkout
# that turned those newlines into CRLF would make the signature fail to verify,
# which is the signature working correctly on the wrong question.
src-tauri/tests/patch-sheet.css -text
src-tauri/tests/patch-sheet.sig.b64 -text
src-tauri/tests/patch-key.pub.b64 -text
